==============================================================================
single_limit=360, two_swap_limit=42, alias_depth=6, lcm_tail_max=8, workers=4
[0] Assumption challenge
  considered vertices:
    runners, q-threshold gaps, strict safe components, C27 shell aliases,
    unital/affine packets, K33 minors, lcm tails, impostor tournaments,
    and proof/disproof obligations.
  chosen vertices:
    adversarial candidate families and the proof route that defeats each one.
  preserved LRC predicate:
    exact M(S) >= 1/14, with strict Haar/Baire safe mass and packet labels
    retained until the row is discharged.
  challenged assumptions:
    (1) a C27 shell label alone proves anything; aliases refute that.
    (2) a tournament iso or floor-odd shadow characterizes tightness.
    (3) positive Haar mass alone can replace owner/carry addresses.

